{"Title":"An Act relative to facilities grants for approved projects under the school building assistance program ","BillNumber":"H574","DocketNumber":"HD441","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AJS1","Name":"Adam J. Scanlon","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T09:53:50.977"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AJS1","Name":"Adam J. Scanlon","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-13T09:53:50.9766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H574/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Scanlon of North Attleborough, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 574) of Adam Scanlon relative to facilities grants for approved projects under the school building assistance program.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tParagraph (C) of subsection (a) of section 10 of chapter 70B of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following sentence:- Up to 6 incentive points may be awarded to districts located within municipalities that have adopted a smart growth zoning district or starter home zoning district, as defined in section 2 of chapter 40R.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}